From: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: compose tunnel underlays and LWT routes

Build the IP-in-IPv6 outer header from the routed forward path, including
one outer 802.1Q tag and an optional PPPoE session. Share the tunnel L3
interface at the physical port for Ethernet/VLAN underlays, or attach it to
the existing lifecycle-owned PPPoE session as the vendor transaction does.

Consume the generic flow action's LWT type, TX tunnel key and reversed
encapsulated-address match to publish fixed IPv4-in-IPv6 LWT flows through
the PPE tunnel transaction.

Merged from:
  0514-08-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-compose-tunnel-underlays.patch
  0514-09-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-offload-ip6-lwt-tunnels.patch

Based on work by:
  Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>

Signed-off-by: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

